{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/86152-practical-organisation-factions","id":86152,"title":"practical organisation factions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-07T11:51:33-08:00","id":86152,"title":"practical organisation factions","content":"Is there any info on practical factions? I mean in the line of functional organisation models. Factions like field investigation, balistics, forensic pathology, information retrieval etc. Everything that could be supportive to your hunters during your investigation. Most hunter factions as written seem to be more ideological. For example the Null Mysteriis are divided in believers (Mulder), non-believers (Scully) and doomsayers (Frank Black). Is there something more practical? Maybe Orpheus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T12:08:06-08:00","id":86165,"title":"","content":"Cheiron Group and Ashwood Abbey have had some sort of hierarchical structure established, as does the Union. Unions, for example, have &quot;Union Reps&quot; that travel around or focus on a certain area, and help start up cells. They also provide backup when needed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cheiron has handlers that watch over cells, reporting back to their bureaucratic overlords about how the Hunt went, who's got potential and who's just chaff on the wind.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey is a pyramid scheme. An existing club hands out a license to another club, which pays fees to the licensing club. The club that was licensed does the same to another club...and another club...and another club.... It all goes somewhere up the chain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:08:25-08:00","id":86252,"title":"","content":"As a <u>general rule</u>, there are exceptions, a Compact will have people like the PCs who are known for their skill in a certain area and ways of getting their names to the people who need their help. You're a Null Mysteriis vampire scientist and you need to know about werewolves fast; you'll be put in touch with someone who's &quot;the PC of another story&quot; and knows about werewolves. To put it another way, most members of the Null Mysteriis will be doing heroic hunterish field work. There's not much room for things like like Cheiron where the doctor never leaves the safety of the lab.<br /> <br /> A Conspiracy will have people who are more like NPCs, but lots of them and willing to support your PCs. Cheiron has lawyers, scientists, managers, PR people, more, none of whom will join you on the field with guns, but will (if management thinks you're worth it) give you vital support.<br /> <br /> <br /> So to conclude: The reason why you don't really see things like &quot;balistics&quot; in the factions is simple: In Null Mysteriis the guy doing ballistics is also doing chemistry, forensic photography, interviews, lab studies and filming witches with a telescopic camera. In short, he's a &quot;PC of another story&quot; and thus his ideological faction matters more than his skill dots. In TF:V the ballistics guy is an NPC, so he doesn't get a faction because factions are for PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/86152-practical-organisation-factions#post86152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example the Null Mysteriis are divided in believers (Mulder), non-believers (Scully) and doomsayers (Frank Black). Is there something more practical? Maybe Orpheus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pet peave of mine. Rationalists and Open Minds both believe in the supernatural. It's just that Rationalists only believe in the supernatural that Null Mysteriis has seen and documented, Open Minds believe in things that haven't been demonstrated to exist yet.<br /> <br /> Rationalist: We know things have Spirits, but that doesn't prove that Gaia is a spirit.<br /> Open Minds: We know that Spirits exist, obviously the Native Americans were right. Lets go to the library and look up the sacred dances, there must be one that will fix global warming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:19:12-08:00","id":87120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/86152-practical-organisation-factions?p=86252#post86252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pet peave of mine. Rationalists and Open Minds both believe in the supernatural. It's just that Rationalists only believe in the supernatural that Null Mysteriis has seen and documented, Open Minds believe in things that haven't been demonstrated to exist yet.<br /> <br /> Rationalist: We know things have Spirits, but that doesn't prove that Gaia is a spirit.<br /> Open Minds: We know that Spirits exist, obviously the Native Americans were right. Lets go to the library and look up the sacred dances, there must be one that will fix global warming!</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean. New WoD (and old WoD too) seems to be designed with factions (both internal and external) who all have their own beliefs and want their vision to be put into practice. To achieve this it always results into politics. Now I like the WoD and maybe I am weird, but I might be more into the Cthulhu/Dark Matter/Conspiracy X crowd. I don't really care for all the backbiting and politics. I just want to do some investigative horror and an organisation like the Hoffmann Institute supports that a little better than most WoD factions. It doesn't really matter that much, because I enjoy it anyway and their are plenty of things I can use, but ... well maybe the things the WoD crowd thinks is really good about their games, are the same things I think are it's weak points. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T10:10:18-07:00","id":90305,"title":"","content":"Found it! It's in Tales of the 13th Precinct. Combine that stuff with Task Force Valkyrie or even better VASCU. Yep!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}